{"slug":"cpi-2024-general-divisions","path":"official","kind":"timeseries","page_url":"https://esankhyiki.mospi.gov.in/macroindicators?product=cpi","frequency":"M","graph":"line","title":"CPI (Base 2024=100): General Index and Divisions","description":"India's consumer price index on MoSPI's new base (2024=100): all-India general index for rural, urban and combined, and the 12 COICOP divisions (food & beverages, clothing, housing/utilities/fuels, transport, health, education, ...). Monthly, index points, plus the official year-on-year inflation rate MoSPI publishes (from January 2026, when a year-earlier index exists). This is the series that replaced the stalled 2012-base 'Miscellaneous' and 'Miscellaneous Rural' pages; the new classification has no 'Miscellaneous' group (its closest counterpart, division 12, 'Personal care, social protection and miscellaneous goods and services', is much narrower), so the series are not interchangeable. The new CPI (base 2024=100, MoSPI, first released 12 Feb 2026 for January 2026) replaced the 2012-base series. It uses the COICOP-2018 classification (12 divisions) and a 358-item basket weighted from the 2023-24 Household Consumption Expenditure Survey, so its groups are NOT comparable with the old Food/Fuel/Clothing/Housing/Miscellaneous groups and it has no 'core' aggregate. Index values start in January 2025 (the base year). Do not chain this series to the 2012-base series.","headline":{},"source":"MoSPI (eSankhyiki CPI, base 2024=100)","source_url":"https://esankhyiki.mospi.gov.in/macroindicators?product=cpi","date_modified":null,"views":[{"id":"general","label":"General index (All India)","series":[{"id":"gen_combined","name":"Combined","units":"Index (2024=100)","pts":[[1735689600,101.67],[1738368000,101.32],[1740787200,101.39],[1743465600,101.58],[1746057600,101.9],[1748736000,102.51],[1751328000,103.35],[1754006400,103.74],[1756684800,103.74],[1759276800,103.74],[1761955200,104.01],[1764547200,104.1],[1767225600,104.45],[1